**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests`

**How to implement.** The app runs on the library database (001 §C, §G; .spec-md §0.1 `AppContext.create`: it composes the SQLite library proxies over the configured locations; §3.9; §7: a mismatch is `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr`). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: `create` becomes `static member create (locations : DataLocations) (settings : WorkbenchSettings) : Result<AppContext, StorageError>`. It opens `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate locations.libraryConnection` (step 62) and answers an error as it is, so a library of another schema is shown and never silently recreated. Over the open database it composes the stores: `materials` = `MaterialProxy.createInDatabase` (step 69), `samples` = `SampleProxy.createInDatabase` (step 74), `sources` = `SourceProxy.createInDatabase` (step 76), `categories` = `CategoryProxy.createInDatabase` (step 71) and `library` = `LibraryProxy.createInDatabase` (step 79). When `database.origin` is `CreatedLibraryDatabase` (step 84) it imports the shipped Built-in catalogue, `(CatalogueImportProxy.ofStores categories materials samples (LibraryEntryStore.createInDatabase database)).importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltInUnder locations.shippedCatalogueFolder)` (steps 80, 81); an `Error e` is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying `e.describe`, and the app starts with what was imported, as step 44 does. An opened library is not imported again: importing on every start, by manifest hash, is S3.1's. `experiments`, `experimentData`, `experimentCollections`, `scenes`, `experimentExport` and `settings` are as in step 83. The in-memory store construction and `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory` go from `create`, with the opens nothing needs any more. The `create` doc says, in one to three lines, that it opens or creates the configured library database, imports the Built-in catalogue into a new one and answers an open failure (001 §C; spec 0050 S2.4); the record and field docs that say in-memory store say database store. (2) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`: `Startup.context` (`Program.fs:59`) is now the `Result`. `LauncherWindow(context : AppContext)` (`Program.fs:134`) becomes `LauncherWindow(opened : Result<AppContext, StorageError>)`, and `App.OnFrameworkInitializationCompleted` (`Program.fs:216`) passes `Startup.context`. On `Ok context` it is today's launcher. On `Error e` it shows, between the title and the buttons, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `ConstructorUiId.launcherLibraryErrorText` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`, with the text `The library could not be opened: <e.describe>`, and the four surface buttons are built with `IsEnabled` false and no click handler, because no window opens without the library. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the launcher group (`UiIds.fs:588-594`): `static member launcherLibraryErrorText : ConstructorUiId = ConstructorUiId "LauncherLibraryErrorText"` with a one-line doc. (4) Tests. `TestAppScope.freshAppContext` (step 83) answers the `Ok` context and fails the calling fact with the error's `describe` otherwise; each call opens its own `:memory:` library, so every composition over it runs on the database with the Built-in catalogue imported. `TestAppScope` gains `fileLocations (owner : FolderName) : DataLocations`: every location of `testLocations` moved into a fresh folder under the owner's (a GUID name, so no run meets another's files), and `libraryConnection` `Data Source=<that folder>/library.db`. `LauncherTests.withLauncher` passes `Ok (freshAppContext …)`, and `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`' `LauncherWindow(ctx)` becomes `LauncherWindow(Ok ctx)`. `TableAndElementRotationTests`, `WireUiCompositionTests` and `WireUi0040CompositionTests` compose through `TestAppScope.freshAppContext` since step 83 and keep their code; their facts now run on the database. `AppContextTests` gains `create imports the Built-in catalogue into a new library database file and a reopen does not import again`: two `AppContext.create` over the same `fileLocations`; the first lists every Built-in sample, and a Built-in sample is removed through it; the second, over the same file, does not list that sample, so it opened the library without importing again, and lists every other Built-in sample. And `create answers LibrarySchemaMismatchErr for a library of another schema and leaves the file as it was`: a file library is created through `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate` and disposed, and its stamp set to 2 through a plain `SqliteConnection` (pooling off); `AppContext.create` over it answers `Error (LibrarySchemaMismatchErr _)`, and the stamp is still 2. `LauncherTests` gains `a library that fails to open is shown on the launcher and the four buttons are disabled`: `LauncherWindow(Error (LibrarySchemaMismatchErr { foundOpt = Some (LibrarySchemaVersion 2); expected = LibrarySchemaVersion.current }))` shows `launcherLibraryErrorText` naming both versions, each of the four buttons is disabled, and raising `Click` on Main opens no window.

**Acceptance.** After the switch, `AppContext.create` MUST answer `Result<AppContext, StorageError>` over the configured library database, and `AppContext.fs` MUST NOT call `MaterialProxy.createInMemory`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory`, `CategoryProxy.createInMemory`, `SourceProxy.createInMemory` or `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `create imports the Built-in catalogue into a new library database file and a reopen does not import again`, `create answers LibrarySchemaMismatchErr for a library of another schema and leaves the file as it was` and `a library that fails to open is shown on the launcher and the four buttons are disabled`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.
